// results-data/amzn.js — Amazon (AMZN) dataset for the standardized "Results" tab.
//
// LAST UPDATED: 17 Aug 2026 — moved onto the v2 VINTAGE AXIS (docs/RESULTS_CONVENTIONS.md §8).
//
// Compares REPORTED actuals against three references, per period:
//   summit  — Summit DCF model estimate. The hand-authored `summit` array is the projection the
//             model FROZE at each print, and it stays authoritative on any period that has
//             already reported. `estMatrix.summit` adds the whole vintage axis on top: 7 saved
//             model files, Dec 2025 → Aug 2026, generated from the Summit MCP.
//   cons    — Street consensus going in. The hand-authored `cons` array is the pre-print number
//             for reported quarters: Refinitiv (1Q–2Q23) / LSEG (3Q23 on) via CNBC earnings-day
//             coverage, AWS per StreetAccount. `estMatrix.cons` adds 30 Bloomberg snapshots back
//             to Apr 2019 — which is what finally gives the SEGMENT lines a consensus history.
//   guideLo / guideHi — Amazon's own guidance range for that quarter, from the prior
//             quarter's press release (8-K Ex. 99.1 on SEC EDGAR). Amazon guides net
//             sales + GAAP operating income only; null for metrics it does not guide.
//
// ── THE VINTAGE AXIS, AND WHY THE FLAT ARRAYS STAY ────────────────────────────────────────────
// `estMatrix` is GENERATED (scripts/consensus/) and must never be hand-edited. It ADDS to this
// dataset and never subtracts from it: on an already-reported period the flat value above wins
// (it is the number frozen at that print, and a snapshot is only ever as fresh as the day it was
// saved), and where no snapshot reaches back far enough the flat value is kept rather than
// blanked. Forward periods take the newest snapshot, which is why the forward columns here now
// read post-2Q26-print rather than the pre-print figures they shipped with in July.
//
// ⚠ ONE SERIES IS DELIBERATELY MISSING. The Bloomberg workbook's ANNUAL North-America revenue
// cell has reprinted the same three numbers since May 2021, relabelling them a year forward at
// each print — 27 distinct values across 90 cells. It is not a time series and is excluded from
// the matrix (see `drop` in scripts/consensus/map_amzn.json). Its QUARTERLY twin moves normally
// and is used. Raise the dead cell with San/Oscar.
//
// All monetary values in US$ millions; EPS in dollars. null = not available.
// Arrays are parallel to `periods`. A period with act:null is an upcoming print.

